@@ -126,6 +126,12 @@ Set `core.SaveOptions.Accept` to validate the chosen destination before writing.
 
 In headless tests, `App.PickFiles`, `App.PickDirectories` and `App.SaveFile` receive `nsgotest.FilePick`, `nsgotest.DirectoryPick` and `nsgotest.FileSave` records. The same records are in `app.FilePicks`, `app.DirectoryPicks` and `app.Saves`.
 
+### Saving photos
+
+Use `mobile.SavePhoto(cx, mobile.PhotoSaveOptions{Name: "photo.jpg", Path: path}, done)` to add an encoded image to the device's photo library on iOS and Android. Supply `Data` instead of `Path` for bytes; `MIME` defaults to the name's extension. The callback `func(saved bool, path string, err error)` runs on the engine goroutine after the library finishes, with a MediaStore URI on Android. iOS preserves the image's original format, including GIF animation.
+
+On iOS, put `NSPhotoLibraryAddUsageDescription` in `apple.info`; the service asks only for permission to add photos. Android 28 requires `android.permission.WRITE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE` in `android.permissions` and asks for it when saving. Android 29 and later need no storage permission. Access denial and write failures report an error. Other platforms report that photo library saving is unavailable; use `cx.SaveFile` for a desktop save dialog.
+
 ### Bundled assets
 
 Put files under the app's `resources/` directory and use `cx.ReadAsset("asset:maps/level.bin", done)` to read them from Go. The callback receives `([]byte, error)` on the engine's goroutine after the read and is dropped if its owner goes away or runs again. Use `errors.Is(err, core.ErrAssetNotFound)` to identify missing files. The read loads the entire file into memory.
